      <!-- ── WHAT THIS IS ── -->
      <h2 id="what-this-is">WHAT THIS IS</h2>

      <p>
        <code>brain</code> is a <strong>knowledge-first execution layer</strong> that sits in front of any terminal process. Before a command runs, before logs are read, before any file is opened — the brain performs a <strong>visual orientation check</strong>: it maps the incoming event to a known stage, surfaces the exact code reference, and tells you <em>what is likely happening</em> before you have to look.
      </p>

      <p>The result:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Answers come faster (you already know where to look)</li>
        <li>Code is easier to read (you know what you're looking for)</li>
        <li>Debugging is narrowed to a single node before you open a file</li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote>
        <p><strong>One rule:</strong> Everything that happens in the system passes through the brain first.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <!-- ── THE CORE IDEA ── -->
      <h2 id="the-core-idea">THE CORE IDEA</h2>

      <p>Without a brain:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrapper">
        <div class="code-block-header">
          <span class="code-block-lang">flow</span>
          <div class="code-block-dots"><span class="dot-red"></span><span class="dot-amber"></span><span class="dot-green"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block-body">
          <pre><code><span class="tok-arrow">Event</span> <span style="color:#6e7681">→</span> <span class="tok-string">Read all logs</span> <span style="color:#6e7681">→</span> <span class="tok-string">Guess the stage</span> <span style="color:#6e7681">→</span> <span class="tok-string">Search codebase</span> <span style="color:#6e7681">→</span> <span class="tok-string">Answer</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>With a brain:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrapper">
        <div class="code-block-header">
          <span class="code-block-lang">flow</span>
          <div class="code-block-dots"><span class="dot-red"></span><span class="dot-amber"></span><span class="dot-green"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block-body">
          <pre><code><span class="tok-arrow">Event</span> <span style="color:var(--accent)">→</span> <span style="color:#3fb950">Brain matches stage</span> <span style="color:var(--accent)">→</span> <span style="color:#3fb950">Surfaces CodeRef</span> <span style="color:var(--accent)">→</span> <span style="color:#3fb950">Focused answer</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>The brain does not execute anything. It <strong>intercepts, maps, and orients</strong> — then hands off to the actual runner.</p>

